Subject: the module majors are the booted manifest's major records

A module's majors were checked against a table compiled into the kernel,
so a new major needed a new kernel.  kbootset now writes one record per
registry row into the manifest ("major <c|b> <n> <name>", C3-5 version
22), and dlm_majowned and md_majors read them there.  A manifest without
the records refuses every major; a malformed row, one past the switch,
or one number in two rows refuses the whole table.  Without a booted
manifest (no module loads then) the built-in table still answers.

--- a/dlm_core.c
+++ b/dlm_core.c
